messages:
Haptics: my probes show a slope of about 0.0031 N per mm³, with 295 mm³ giving 0.901 N, 305 giving 0.932 and 330 giving 1.008. I'm cutting from 315 to 300 mm³, which should give about 0.916 N and frees 15 mm³. I won't go to 295, because the 0.901 N there leaves almost no margin against the 0.9 N floor. This round I'm probing 290, 297 and 300 to confirm the floor.

My requirement is met, but haptics is only about 3% of the interior, so this barely dents the overage of about 994 mm³. The big cuts have to come from:
- structure: ribs 1400 and a smaller port;
- acoustics: 200-400 mm³;
- NFC: its floor;
- battery or antenna: whatever their slopes allow.

I OBJECT while the interior is over-committed.
